githubusercontent.com/u/4139006?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp","html_url":"https://github.com/bsdimp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-24T20:00:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T20:00:31Z","body":"Help me understand, what's the difference betweeen 'this list of conditions' and 'the entire permission notice'?  What's in one that's not in the other? Is it because neither of these terms are well defined in law universally enough to consider them the same, or some other reason?\n\nSince the legal folks say that they are different, I'm +1 to accept this (even though I'm asking questions to understand why). Is Ted Tso the real originator, or just the first example that's come to light?\n\nSide note: The FreeBSD ports/packages tree is about to transition from home-baked identifiers to the SPDX specified ones. I'm trying to provide guidance to the people writing the policy to help advise them when things are 'different enough' to matter. I think in this case, the use of different terms, though they seem to be synonymous, could be a problem because neither is defined in law....","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3114755140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused